          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "MeitY Tightens AI Labelling Rules for India, Mandates Continuous Disclosure of AI-Generated Content",
            "articleSection": "Policy & Rights",
            "abstract": "India's Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology (MeitY) has issued updated regulations requiring platforms to apply continuous disclosure labels to AI-generated content, going beyond one-time labelling at upload. The new rules tighten accountability for platforms hosting synthetic media and are part of India's broader push to regulate AI outputs in public-facing digital spaces. This move follows growing global concern around AI-generated misinformation and deepfakes circulating on Indian social media platforms.",
            "url": "https://www.medianama.com/2026/04/223-meity-ai-label-rules-mandates-continuous-disclosure/",
            "publisher": {
              "@type": "NewsMediaOrganization",
              "name": "The AI Chronicle",
              "url": "https://theaichronicle.com",
              "logo": {
